chart hbar fleet y=five-year cost unit=$ labels title="Five-year cost for the 18-van fleet"

## Risks

- **Electric range.** Real-world range is about 180 miles in summer and 150 in winter. Our longest route is 140 miles a day, so the electric van is tight on the longest two routes in January. We can charge overnight at the depot with 6 chargers.
- **Hybrid emissions.** Hybrids have no range worries, but they still produce tailpipe emissions.
- **Diesel fee.** Diesel vans are subject to the city low-emission zone fee of $12.50 a day, starting 2028-01-01.

## Recommendation

Buy electric vans for the 12 shorter routes, and hybrids for the 6 longest. This mixed fleet comes to $1,609,800 for the 18 vans over five years, about $316,200 less than staying with diesel. All-electric is cheaper on paper, at $1,555,200, but its range is tight on the longest routes.
